    "abstract": "Parts breakdown of the cabin floor proximity marking, showing the exit marker assemblies, the lining panel that carries the strip channel and the attachment set common to the aisle run.",
    "sections": {
      "purpose": "This figure gives the parts breakdown of the cabin floor proximity escape path marking along both aisles and around the exits.",
      "figure_note": "Sheet 1 shows the left aisle from the forward exit to the mid cabin; sheet 2 covers the exit surrounds. Item 20 is the exit marker assembly. Two marking families are in service and both are ordered against this item; a note on sheet 2 gives the family fitted at each exit and the reader is expected to check the aircraft configuration record before ordering. The attachment set at items 40 and 60 is shown once and is used by both families. The lining panel at item 30 carries the strip channel and is common to both standards, but a panel with a broken channel lip must be replaced rather than reused."
    },
