    "abstract": "Parts breakdown of the cabin floor proximity marking, showing the exit marker assemblies in the photoluminescent and the light-emitting diode standards and the lining panel that carries the strip channel.",
    "sections": {
      "purpose": "This figure gives the parts breakdown of the cabin floor proximity escape path marking along both aisles and around the exits.",
      "figure_note": "Sheet 1 shows the left aisle from the forward exit to the mid cabin; sheet 2 covers the exit surrounds. Items 20 and 20A are the two marker standards and must never be mixed on one aisle. The attachment set follows the marker and is no longer common: the photoluminescent marker is packed out on tubular spacers at item 40, the diode marker is screwed to the panel at item 40A and anchored with the nuts at item 60, and the two arrangements have different hole positions in the panel. The note that used to carry this distinction on sheet 2 is deleted; the effectivity is now on the items themselves, because the mixed fleet will last past 2028 and a note is not a reliable place for information an ordering system has to read. The lining panel at item 30 carries the strip channel and is common to both standards, but a panel with a broken channel lip must be replaced rather than reused."
    },
